  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**What this dashboard answers:** what is being done to memories, by whom, and how often it fails.\n\n* Source: Prometheus counters `memory_operations_total`, `memory_operation_errors_total`, `memory_retrieve_total` and `memory_retrieve_hits_total`. Aggregates only: no query text or memory IDs.\n* **CRUD Operations Rate / Cumulative:** volume per operation. Use the cumulative view to see totals since the server started; the rate view to spot bursts.\n* **Operation Error Rate / Error Rate (fraction):** failures per operation, and failures divided by calls. Any sustained fraction above ~0.01 deserves a look at the server logs for that operation.\n* **Memory Retrieve Hit Rate / Volume:** hit rate = search/retrieve calls with at least one result divided by all calls. It counts calls, not result quality. A falling hit rate means more empty answers. Next: **Mem0 — Query Misses** lists the queries behind it.\n* **Top Memory Operations by User:** the 10 busiest `operation` + `user_id` pairs. In pi, `user_id` is `<user>:project:<hash>`, so this is effectively the busiest projects.\n* To see which memories are hit most, open **Mem0 — Hot Memories**."
      }
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10
      },
      "id": 1,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Operation Volumes",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "CRUD Operations Rate",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 11
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "rate(memory_operations_total[$__rate_interval])",
          "legendFormat": "{{operation}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Operations per second by operation, user_id and agent_id. Use it to spot bursts.\n\n**Read:** operations per second (add, search, update, delete...).\n\n**Look for:** bursts and unexpected operations.\n\n**Example:** a spike of `add` with no `search` = capture running without recall."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "CRUD Operations — Cumulative",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 11
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "lineInterpolation": "stepAfter"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "last"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (operation) (memory_operations_total)",
          "legendFormat": "{{operation}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Total operations since the server started, per operation.\n\n**Read:** running total since the server started, per operation.\n\n**Look for:** the ratio search : add.\n\n**Example:** resets to 0 after a server restart; it is not a bug."
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 19
      },
      "id": 4,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Errors & Hit Rate",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Operation Error Rate",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 20
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "cps",
          "custom": {
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth"
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "rate(memory_operation_errors_total[$__rate_interval])",
          "legendFormat": "{{operation}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Failed operations per second by operation.\n\n**Read:** failed operations per second.\n\n**Look for:** any sustained line.\n\n**Example:** `add` errors rising after a deploy = check the LLM/embedding provider key in the server logs."
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "Error Rate (fraction of operations)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 20
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1,
          "custom": {
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth"
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "rate(memory_operation_errors_total[$__rate_interval]) / rate(memory_operations_total[$__rate_interval])",
          "legendFormat": "error fraction",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Failures divided by calls. Sustained values above ~0.01 deserve a look at the server logs for that operation.\n\n**Read:** failures divided by calls per operation.\n\n**Look for:** sustained values above ~0.01.\n\n**Example:** 0.5 on `update` = half of the edits fail."
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "title": "Memory Retrieve Hit Rate",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1,
          "custom": {
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "last"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "rate(memory_retrieve_hits_total[$__rate_interval]) / rate(memory_retrieve_total[$__rate_interval])",
          "legendFormat": "hit rate",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Search/retrieve calls with at least one result divided by all such calls. Counts calls, not result quality.\n\n**Read:** share of search/retrieve calls that returned at least one result.\n\n**Look for:** a drop = more empty answers; see Query Misses for which queries.\n\n**Example:** 0.9 -> 0.6 after switching a project's scope."
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "title": "Retrieve Volume (hits vs total)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 28
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "cps",
          "custom": {
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "last"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "rate(memory_retrieve_total[$__rate_interval])",
          "legendFormat": "total retrieves",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "rate(memory_retrieve_hits_total[$__rate_interval])",
          "legendFormat": "hits",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Search/retrieve calls per second: all calls versus calls that returned results. The gap is the number of empty answers.\n\n**Read:** all search/retrieve calls vs those with results; the gap is empty answers.\n\n**Look for:** the two lines diverging.\n\n**Example:** total 2/s vs hits 1/s = half of calls return nothing."
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 36
      },
      "id": 9,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Top Operations by User",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "title": "Top Memory Operations by User",
      "type": "table",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 37
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "align": "auto"
          },
          "displayMode": "auto"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "footer": {
          "show": false
        },
        "sortBy": [
          {
            "displayName": "Value",
            "desc": true
          }
        ]
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "topk(10, sum by (operation, user_id) (rate(memory_operations_total[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{operation}} — {{user_id}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true
            },
            "indexByName": {},
            "renameByName": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "The 10 busiest operation + user_id pairs. In pi, user_id ends with the project hash, so this is the busiest projects.\n\n**Read:** busiest operation + user_id pairs; user_id ends with the project hash.\n\n**Look for:** which project generates most traffic.\n\n**Example:** one project with 10x the `search` rate of the others is a looping agent or heavy user."
    }
  ]
}